## PROJECT IDENTITY
This is a MERN stack web application.
Frontend: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS
Backend: Node.js + Express.js
Database: MongoDB Atlas + Mongoose
Deployment: Vercel (frontend) + Render (backend)
Package manager: npm

## FOLDER STRUCTURE
Root contains two folders:
- /client — React frontend (ES modules, import/export)
- /server — Express backend (CommonJS, require/module.exports)

Never create files outside of /client or /server unless I ask.
Never mix CommonJS and ES modules in the same folder.

## NAMING CONVENTIONS
- React components: PascalCase (UserCard.jsx, AdminDashboard.jsx)
- Utility files: camelCase (calculateBills.js, sendEmail.js)
- Route files: camelCase (auth.js, tenants.js)
- MongoDB models: PascalCase singular (Tenant.js, MonthlyBill.js)
- CSS classes: Tailwind utility classes only — no custom class names unless necessary
- Environment variables: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (MONGODB_URI, JWT_SECRET)

## CODE CONVENTIONS
Backend (/server):
- CommonJS only: const x = require('x') and module.exports = {}
- All routes wrapped in try/catch
- Response format always: { success: Boolean, message: String, data: any }
- All secrets via process.env — never hardcoded
- Mongoose models in /server/models/
- Route handlers in /server/routes/
- Reusable logic in /server/utils/

Frontend (/client):
- ES modules only: import / export
- All API calls through /client/src/api/axios.js
- Tailwind CSS only for styling
- React Router for all navigation
- No inline style objects unless absolutely necessary

## FILES TO NEVER TOUCH
- .env (never read, never write, never show contents)
- package-lock.json
- node_modules/
- dist/ or build/

## DEPENDENCIES ALREADY INSTALLED
Server: express, mongoose, jsonwebtoken, bcryptjs, nodemailer,
        multer, cloudinary, date-fns-tz, cors, dotenv
Client: react, react-dom, react-router-dom, axios,
        tailwindcss, date-fns, pdfmake

Do not suggest installing a library that is already in this list.
Do not suggest a paid library or service.
